From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sebastian Matkovich <sebastian.matkovich@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 21:59:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] qcom_wdt: feed every 15 s with slack

The watchdog bites after about 32 s; feeding it every 5 s woke the CPU
twice as often as needed. Every 15 s, with 5 s of slack for the callout
to ride along with other wake-ups (the N9's dsme kicked its watchdog on
the shared IP heartbeat).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sys/dev/qcom_wdt/qcom_wdt.c | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sys/dev/qcom_wdt/qcom_wdt.c b/sys/dev/qcom_wdt/qcom_wdt.c
index 9cb5cb912..c5c03d8bf 100644
--- a/sys/dev/qcom_wdt/qcom_wdt.c
+++ b/sys/dev/qcom_wdt/qcom_wdt.c
@@ -36,7 +36,13 @@
 #define	WDT_BITE_TIME	0x14
 #define	WDT_ENABLE	(1u << 0)
 #define	WDT_MAX_TICKS	0xfffff		/* about 32 s of the 32 kHz clock */
-#define	WDT_FEED_S	5
+/*
+ * Fed every 15 s, with 5 s of slack so that the feed can ride along with
+ * other wake-ups (it bites after about 32 s): fewer wake-ups than every
+ * 5 s, as the N9's dsme kept its watchdog kicks on the shared heartbeat
+ */
+#define	WDT_FEED_S	15
+#define	WDT_FEED_SLACK_S 5
 
 static struct ofw_compat_data compat_data[] = {
 	{ "qcom,apss-wdt-sm6115",	1 },
@@ -62,7 +68,8 @@ qcom_wdt_feed(void *arg)
 		return;
 	}
 	bus_write_4(sc->res, WDT_RST, 1);
-	callout_reset(&sc->feed, WDT_FEED_S * hz, qcom_wdt_feed, sc);
+	callout_reset_sbt(&sc->feed, WDT_FEED_S * SBT_1S,
+	    WDT_FEED_SLACK_S * SBT_1S, qcom_wdt_feed, sc, 0);
 }
 
 static int
